/-!
# RA-20: genuine algebraic critical-point definitions (statement draft)

Formalization author: George Stepaniants, Department of Computing and Mathematical
Sciences, California Institute of Technology, Pasadena, California, USA.
Original negative-resolution mathematics: the Codex automated maintainer audit
retained by OpenProblemsInNLA. The conjecture is due to Kubjas, Sodomaco and Tsigaridas.

The smooth locus below is Mathlib's algebraic smooth locus of the reduced
coordinate ring, not the matrix rank-two stratum or a coordinate-case predicate.
The tangent space uses the entire vanishing ideal. Distances and derivatives are
complex bilinear; they contain no complex conjugation. Genericity means a
nonempty principal Zariski-open set in the full space of symmetric data.
