# RA-20 complete local assembly and conclusion handoff

All twelve exact frozen contracts compile from genuine proofs. The three newly
owned sources are fixed at:

| Source | SHA-256 |
| --- | --- |
| `NLA/RA20/Count.lean` | `99e44e2ec0d376cb346822c8f5a7edcc72c78448083361e5b4f2ea3aceb92c96` |
| `NLA/RA20/Proof.lean` | `d3cb0dab572eb54795e6568c717e9e6f8200eb20f299e319fc3be36bbe8aaea1` |
| `Solution.lean` | `755a58cc081172804c644ea83518581235763a6ecefcbff6c92f131ca44c32b5` |

The Count module proves the genuine cardinality of the actual smooth critical
subtype is three for every datum in `GenericData`. It uses the proved equality
of that entire critical set with the range of the injective three-element
candidate map. The actual cardinal range theorem supplies the equality; no
finite-cardinality convention turns an infinite set into zero.

The generic count of three uses an explicitly nonempty principal open set in
the full symmetric data space. If an arbitrary different nonempty principal
open set had count four, the proved `generic_data_intersection_proved` would
supply a datum in both sets, contradicting equality of the same cardinal with
three and four. Finally `n=s=3` is in the original universal parameter range,
and its original predicted expression equals four. This proves the negation
of the complete four-formula conjecture, without separately deciding the other
three formulas or silently restricting the unknown exceptional polynomial.

Proof and Solution were created only after every substantive imported helper
and Count compiled. `Solution.lean` retains all twelve reviewed types; it imports
the genuine Proof assembly, never Challenge. `wrapper-assembly.json` records
the exact source-generation boundary. A separate namespace-only copy of frozen
Challenge serves solely as an admitted diagnostic reference. The actual export
types all match it by Lean definitional equality, and the actual proofs do not
reach any reference declaration.

## Fresh validation and retained scope

An initially empty private prefix re-elaborated eleven project source modules,
the diagnostic reference and the actual dependency inspector: thirteen
successful commands, about 93 seconds of local command time. The only failed
assembly command was the first Count attempt; finite cardinal and vector
reductions were then made explicit. Both versions and all raw diagnostics are
retained. Two style suggestions already present in sealed Differential remain;
the reference intentionally emits twelve admission warnings. No completed
proof contains an admission.

The actual type/body traversal checks 214 safe project declarations and 39
required mathematical dependencies. It reaches the real reduced ideal,
algebraic smooth locus, entire-ideal tangent condition, complex Fréchet
derivative, generic-open intersection and cardinal subtype count. Sixty-one
source and twelve diagnostic LeanCert kernel assertions pass. The successful
logs contain 57 source and 12 diagnostic printed axiom reports, each exactly
`propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. These counts are distinct:
Algebra has four source assertions without corresponding print commands.
Unsafe or partial project declarations, unknown bodyless declarations,
admissions and nonstandard transitive axioms are rejected by the inspector.

This is pure exact algebra and calculus. LeanCert performs actual kernel trust
auditing; no artificial numerical singleton or interval certificate is added.
The exact ten MI-22 dependencies remained read-only and were rechecked at clean
pinned revisions. No Lake build, dependency download, dependency copy or cache
mutation occurred. After successful inspection, the two completed prefixes
owned by this author were removed: 40 generated `.olean`/`.ilean` files,
8,439,971 logical bytes, each hashed in `owned-prefix-cleanup.json`. All source
and evidence bytes remain. Other authors' prefixes and shared dependencies
were untouched.

The original conclusion ownership record remains unchanged; root explicitly
transferred the three sources before any edit, recorded separately in
`ownership-transfer-2026-09-13.json`. All 68 frozen statement inputs, 16 original
source snapshots/Git blobs, comparator settings and every sealed helper remain
exact. `validation.json` binds successful source hashes, times, results, pins
and inspection counts. The outer assembly manifest retains all seven complete
helper seals and every file they bind, including nested manifests. Only that
outer manifest's exact path is excluded from its own inventory.

