# RA-20 actual generic critical-set classification: complete

`NLA.RA20.generic_critical_locus_proved` proves the exact frozen contract 7 for every complex symmetric datum `U` satisfying the original `GenericData U` predicate. The conclusion is equality of the entire actual smooth critical set with the range of the three prescribed matrices, together with injectivity of that enumeration. Source `NLA/RA20/Critical.lean` is frozen at SHA256 `e8b2e3646d4b1f5e41e35ae4e23ba55d758cb6e48d125643d02eb1d51cab2040`.

The implementation retains the genuine vanishing-ideal tangent space, the actual algebraic smooth locus and the actual complex derivative of the full-entry Frobenius polynomial. It does not replace any of those predicates with a convenient chart definition. The complete smooth-locus theorem first proves that every relevant matrix is hollow with exactly one zero off-diagonal coordinate. The complete tangent theorem then proves that every tangent direction is symmetric and hollow and satisfies the appropriate linear equation; no rank restriction is imposed on tangent directions. The actual full derivative on such a direction is four times the off-diagonal bilinear pairing.

On each of the three smooth planes, testing the two free coordinate directions forces the corresponding two entries to equal those of the datum. Conversely, the product of the other two nonzero coordinates forces the fixed tangent coordinate to vanish, proving criticality against every complex tangent direction. All three proposed matrices are consequently actual smooth critical points, and every actual smooth critical point is one of them. The three nonzero off-diagonal data coordinates also prove pairwise distinctness. The datum's diagonal entries remain arbitrary throughout. These are universal exact algebraic deductions, not a check of one numerical datum.

## Author validation

Nine direct-source Lean commands passed from a new empty prefix: Definitions, Algebra, SmoothTransport, Smooth, Differential, Tangent, Critical, the isolated frozen Challenge, and the exact-contract/dependency inspector. No old RA-20 objects appeared on the Lean path. The reference emitted exactly its twelve intentional placeholder warnings. The sealed Differential import emitted its two previously recorded nonblocking `letI` style warnings; its bytes were preserved. All other implemented sources and the inspector were warning-free.

The actual contract consumer elaborated, and its type was checked definitionally against the exported theorem. The fresh commands executed 30 explicit LeanCert kernel assertions and printed 26 standard-three axiom reports. The actual type/body traversal reached 174 project declarations and required 39 material semantic dependencies, including the full smoothness, entire-ideal tangent, infinitesimal lifting, reduced-coordinate-ring and full-derivative chains. No reached project declaration was unsafe, partial, bodyless or dependent on an extra axiom. The accepted pure exact proof scope uses LeanCert's kernel trust audit without manufacturing an unused interval certificate.

The fresh result is `final-f7_nxk8d/result.json`, SHA256 `9747fe1843f71237e97342a17fe53f12b3177f0289955fb01d20eeebe127ae10`. All development attempts retain their exact source snapshots, complete raw logs, commands, outcomes and object hashes. The first attempt failed only in a redundant finite-matrix symmetry helper; the final implementation uses the separately proved generic helper from Tangent. No frozen statement, definition or mathematical target changed.

All 68 frozen statement inputs, 16 original immutable Git sources, and six imported source files were rehashed unchanged. All five imported helper evidence inventories were also rechecked in full, including their nested manifests. Ten exact dependency revisions remained clean and were reused read-only from MI-22. No Lake build, download or dependency copy was performed. Only the two owned generated Critical prefixes were hash-recorded and removed. The evidence manifest includes every own raw attempt, the handoff and exact source/import identities, and excludes only its own outer file.

This is implementation-author validation on macOS. It is not an additional independent mathematical referee, actual Ubuntu replay, Comparator result or publication approval. The complete RA-20 assembly and independent final review/Linux gates remain separately recorded.

Implementation owner is `/root/leancert_examples`, who also authored Smooth and is therefore ineligible as an independent final mathematical referee. The earlier independent statement review remains historical. Algebra and Tangent retain `/root/formal_review_standards` implementation attribution, Differential retains `/root/mf16_final_referee` attribution, and SmoothTransport retains `/root` attribution. Reused Mathlib results retain their original source credit.

