# RA-20 genuine smooth-locus helper: complete

`NLA.RA20.algebraic_smooth_locus_proved` proves the exact frozen contract 3 for every complex 3-by-3 matrix. It identifies the actual `SmoothPoint 3 3 X` with the prescribed hollow form and exactly one zero off-diagonal coordinate. The actual vanishing-ideal quotient, point prime, local ring and algebraic formal-smoothness predicate are retained. The origin and every coordinate-axis intersection are excluded by proof, including intersections whose matrices have rank two.

Source `NLA/RA20/Smooth.lean` is frozen at SHA256 `99ab24934f75382e9bad4a8e84945d0f1e14123804d5172a66b0da17a9eceb88` (23,808 bytes). Its source should remain unchanged during integration unless an explicit amendment is coordinated. Implementation owner `/root/leancert_examples` wrote this module after the accepted two-review statement gate; the earlier independent statement review remains historical. The implementer is ineligible as an independent final mathematical referee.

## Actual algebraic argument

The polynomial ring localized at the preimage of the quotient point maps onto the actual local ring of `C[a,b,c]/(abc)`. `abcLocalizationMap_surjective` and `abcLocalizationMap_ker` derive surjectivity and the principal kernel from the pinned localization APIs.

The generic `triple_product_not_formallySmooth` uses Mathlib's infinitesimal lifting equivalence. If that quotient were formally smooth, its actual square-zero thickening modulo the square of the presentation kernel would admit a section. Representatives of the lifted coordinates have the form `a + abc*u`, `b + abc*v`, `c + abc*w`. Multiplying them, using the lifted relation and cancelling the nonzero `abc` in the localized polynomial domain gives an identity whose evaluation at a point with all three pairwise products zero is `1=0`. This establishes the nonsmooth direction without assuming a Jacobian criterion, a regularity theorem or the desired smoothness characterization.

For the converse, evaluation-preserving substitution sets the unique zero coordinate to zero. This polynomial map kills the relation and extends through the quotient and every denominator in the actual prime complement. The other two coordinates are units in the actual local ring, so their product forces the remaining coordinate to vanish there. Consequently the chart gives an actual algebra retraction from the formally smooth localized polynomial ring. `formallySmooth_of_retraction` proves descent of formal smoothness using the genuine infinitesimal lifting property. The construction covers each of the three choices of zero coordinate.

The separately implemented `Algebra.lean` supplies the actual reduced coordinate-ring isomorphism, including its Nullstellensatz and squarefree-ideal proof. The root's sealed `SmoothTransport.lean` transports the genuine local smooth locus along an algebra equivalence. `reducedPoint_comap` identifies the transported evaluation prime in all nine original coordinates, and injectivity of the quotient-prime comap identifies any prime allowed by the original definition. Thus the final contract applies to the original matrix-space predicate, rather than only to an auxiliary quotient.

## Validation and retained evidence

Six commands ran from a new empty prefix: Definitions, Algebra, SmoothTransport, Smooth, the isolated frozen Challenge, and this helper's actual declaration inspector. All passed. The reference emitted exactly its twelve intentional placeholder warnings; the implemented sources and inspector emitted no warnings. The copied exact contract consumer elaborated and its actual type was checked definitionally against the exported theorem.

The source commands executed 16 explicit LeanCert kernel assertions and printed 12 standard-three axiom reports. The actual proof/type traversal reached 111 project declarations and required 30 material dependencies, including the square-zero lifting criterion, localized kernel and surjectivity, local retraction, genuine smoothness transport, complete reduced-ideal bridge and point-prime identification. No project body was unsafe, partial, bodyless or dependent on an extra axiom. Pure exact algebra requires no artificial interval computation or numerical certificate.

The fresh result is `final-_wf6n0_p/result.json`, SHA256 `5b3ffbdd8f3241a6eb6257115e4196c9a13b268f2910d5913aaa8083d5e197eb`. All development attempts, including initial elaboration and inspector failures, retain their exact source snapshots, complete logs, commands and results. Initial failures involved Lean API/coercion spellings, one finite simplification timeout, and the inspector's monad namespace; no frozen definition or target changed. Failed declarations were correctly rejected by kernel-trust assertions. Only the complete final source is the claimed proof.

All 68 frozen statement inputs, 16 original immutable Git sources and the two imported helper sources were rehashed unchanged. Ten exact dependency revisions were checked clean and reused read-only from MI-22, with no old target object, Lake build, download or dependency copy. Both owned generated prefixes were hashed and removed after completion. `PRIMARY-API-IDENTITIES.json` binds the exact pinned library files; the outer evidence manifest includes every nested attempt and excludes only itself.

This is author validation on macOS, not a new independent mathematical review, Linux replay, Comparator success or full RA-20 completion. The remaining contracts, two independent final mathematical referees, actual Ubuntu verification and publication remain separate gates.

